<title>USA: Slow progress in talks-American Airlines official.</title>
<headline>Slow progress in talks-American Airlines official.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Airlines is making slow progress in contract talks with the Allied Pilots Association aimed at heading off a strike, American Airlines spokesman Chris Chiames said.</p>
<p>&quot;Progress is coming but it's coming slowly,&quot; he told a news conference. &quot;Clearly the next few hours are going to be critical to whether we're going to get a deal.&quot;</p>
<p>The union has set a strike deadline of midnight Friday (0500 GMT Saturday).</p>
